---
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/config';
---

<BaseLayout title="Help — How to Use This Knowledge Base" description="How to connect AI agents to rustman.org knowledge base. llms.txt, MCP, skills, API access.">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2 font-mono prompt">Help</h1>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">This site is a knowledge base for AI agents and humans. Here is how to connect.</p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h2>For AI Agents</h2>

    <h3>1. MCP server (connect once, search and read everything)</h3>
    <p>A remote MCP server at <code>https://rustman.org/mcp</code>: Streamable HTTP, no key, no account. Two tools: <code>search</code> across every wiki page, post, project, stack and skill, and <code>read</code>, which returns any page as Markdown.</p>
    <pre><code># Claude Code
claude mcp add --transport http rustman https://rustman.org/mcp

# Claude Desktop, claude.ai, ChatGPT: add a custom connector with this URL
https://rustman.org/mcp

# Cursor and other clients (mcp.json)
{"{"} "mcpServers": {"{"} "rustman": {"{"} "url": "https://rustman.org/mcp" {"}"} {"}"} {"}"}</code></pre>
    <p>Its card is at <a href="/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json">/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json</a>.</p>

    <h3>2. Markdown, without parsing HTML</h3>
    <p>Every page answers <code>Accept: text/markdown</code> with its Markdown twin, and each twin also sits at the page address plus <code>.md</code>. The home page answers with llms.txt.</p>
    <pre><code>curl -H "Accept: text/markdown" https://rustman.org/wiki/harness-engineering-summary/
curl https://rustman.org/llms.txt         # every page: title, URL, description
curl https://rustman.org/llms-full.txt    # every page in full</code></pre>

    <h3>3. Solo Factory skills</h3>
    <pre><code>npx skills add fortunto2/solo-factory/knowledge</code></pre>
    <p>The <code>/knowledge</code> skill loads llms.txt, finds relevant pages, fetches and synthesizes answers. Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini CLI, Codex. All the skills are listed with a digest each in <a href="/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json">/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json</a>.</p>

    <h3>4. Discovery, for agents that look before they ask</h3>
    <p>Every response carries <code>Link</code> headers to the files below, and robots.txt states what AI may do here (search and answers yes, training no).</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/.well-known/api-catalog">/.well-known/api-catalog</a> — the APIs (RFC 9727)</li>
      <li><a href="/.well-known/agent-card.json">/.well-known/agent-card.json</a> — what an agent can do here, and through which interface</li>
      <li><a href="/.well-known/ard.json">/.well-known/ard.json</a> — agentic resources, one entry per skill</li>
      <li><a href="/agents.txt">/agents.txt</a> — the policy in plain words</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>5. Your own knowledge base (Solograph)</h3>
    <p>Not this site: the local tool behind it. Semantic search over your own notes, code graph and session history:</p>
    <pre><code>claude mcp add -s project solograph -- uvx solograph</code></pre>
    <p>See <a href="/projects/project-solograph/">Solograph</a>.</p>

    <h2>For Humans</h2>

    <h3>Search</h3>
    <p>Click the <strong>search icon</strong> in the top nav (or press <kbd>/</kbd>). Searches all content. On section pages, scoped to that section.</p>

    <h3>Browse</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/course/">Course</a> — structured learning path, 7 modules</li>
      <li><a href="/posts/">Posts</a> — pillar articles (methodology, frameworks)</li>
      <li><a href="/wiki/">Wiki</a> — compiled knowledge pages</li>
      <li><a href="/projects/">Projects</a> — build-in-public case studies</li>
      <li><a href="/skills/">Skills</a> — 30+ executable Claude Code skills</li>
      <li><a href="/stacks/">Stacks</a> — technology stack templates</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>RSS</h3>
    <pre><code>https://rustman.org/rss.xml</code></pre>

    <h2>Content Structure</h2>

    <p>Built on <a href="https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f">Karpathy's LLM Wiki pattern</a>: raw sources (immutable) → wiki (LLM-maintained synthesis) → blog (published subset). Files are source of truth, indexes are derived.</p>

    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>What</th><th>URL pattern</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Posts</td><td>Pillar articles from raw sources</td><td><code>/posts/{'{slug}'}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Wiki</td><td>Compiled knowledge pages</td><td><code>/wiki/{'{slug}'}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Projects</td><td>Open source + products</td><td><code>/projects/{'{slug}'}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Skills</td><td>Solo Factory skills (auto-collected)</td><td><code>/skills/{'{slug}'}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Stacks</td><td>YAML stack templates</td><td><code>/stacks/{'{slug}'}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Course</td><td>Structured learning path</td><td><code>/course</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Connect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={SITE.social.github}>GitHub</a> — all projects open source</li>
      <li><a href={SITE.social.telegram}>Telegram</a></li>
      <li><a href={SITE.social.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href={SITE.contact.calendar}>Book a call</a></li>
      <li><EmailLink email={SITE.contact.email} /></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
